   10d. F13: THE TRANSMIT SHARE BOUNDED (FW-B21, drafted)
   With FDCAN_CCCR.DAR = 1 every frame is one the firmware scheduled (10b), so the firmware's schedule alone sets how long each TXD is
   dominant. FW-B21: each supervisor's own TXD dominant at most 2 % of every 100 ms window on each fabric, its frames, their error flags
   and its acknowledgements counted. A transceiver then averages ICC_rec + (ICC_dom - ICC_rec) x 0.02 = 3.5 + (60 - 3.5) x 0.02 = 4.63 mA
   (PRINTED 60 mA dominant at RL 50 Ohm: the bus's least RL is 59.80 Ohm, two ends of 2 x 60R4 at -1 %, between the 50 and 60 Ohm rows,
   the larger taken), under its DECLARED 0.020 A; the declaration holds for ANY dominant current up to 828.5 mA at that share, which covers
   the 180 mA bus-fault row and the 200 mA short-circuit row. The function needs far less: the quorum's frames at 1 Mbit/s or less
   (FW-B09) are a few per 100 ms; the bound is a firmware property the schedule computes, CONFIRMED on the bench by V-B21, not decided there
   The window: the junction follows the window's average when the window is short against the package's thermal time constant, which
   Diodes does not print (MISSING); whatever that constant, the junction never passes the held figure of section 8 (m) (146.4 C on rev Y
   at this air with the enabled set, under the 150 C absolute maximum)
   F13: the held row (m) stays the no-row bound; WITH THE ROW the regulator reads 109.4 C on rev V (inside 125 C) and 125.2 C on rev Y's cover
     (OVER by 0.2 K; a rev X part HELD under L9T5-D7) at 76.25 C, the worst drop's corner

