   10j. THE CHECK cx45's Q3 (focused check of candidate 06077cee, NOT CONFIRMED) AND ITS RECHECK cx46 (of 4d0ff8a2: CORRECTIONS NOT CLOSED,
   the second negative: the method ends; this section is the DISPOSITION, text and predicates, no new design): THE SCHEDULE, THE
   CONTAINMENT DRAFTED, THE QUORUM, THE HEADROOM, THE THERMAL ENVELOPE, THE ROWS (DERIVED on the printed rows; labels as above). Every
   claim below is OPEN or PROVISIONAL; nothing in it is closed; what each handed-over case weakens is said at the claim
   (a) THE MESSAGE SCHEDULE, FW-B22 (drafted in apply_hw_fw_contract_t10.py): per controller and fabric, in every 100 ms window, one state
     frame (its view of the assignment, its health, a sequence count) and at most five event frames; classic 8-byte frames at 500 kbit/s
     or 1 Mbit/s, 135 bit-times each with stuffing (MODEL); a larger change spreads over windows. Its dominant bound, every bit counted
     dominant plus 12 acknowledgements: 822 bit-times against FW-B21's 1000 (2 % of the window at 500 kbit/s; 2000 at 1 Mbit/s): inside;
     the bus 4.9 % loaded at 500 kbit/s; a state frame waits at most 4.6 ms behind every other frame of its window; the quorum's
     2-of-3 decision reads the three state frames of one window: at most 100 ms plus 4.6 ms
     PROVISIONAL (cx46 5): this establishes the traffic MODEL, not a fault-contained quorum service: a TX pin toggled as a GPIO under the
     limiter's share and a latent stuck comparator are admitted counterexamples (L9T5-F21 weakens FW-B22 and CON-004's quorum)
   (b) THE CONTAINMENT DRAFTED (apply_gen_sch_b_iocguard.py, after iocbuck, iocpre and canshdn; NOT APPLIED): two bounds that no firmware
     sets, each acting on one controller only; the rows read (PRINTED): INA169 990 to 1010 uA/V, offset at most 1.0 mV, specified to 85 C;
     TPS3701 VIT-(INB) 387 to 400 mV, VIT+(INB) 397 to 403 mV, its inputs at most 25 nA, OUTB low over VIT+(INB); TCAN334 SHDN VIH 2 V, VIL
     0.8 V, at most 4 uA out of the pin at 0 V
     the response times below are MODEL figures without the comparator's own delay (SBVS240C prints its propagation and start-up delays
     TYPICAL only), with TXD's high level taken as the rail and the frames' least dominant fraction an ASSUMPTION: not maxima
     1. THE TRANSMIT-SHARE LIMITER, one per transceiver: TXD through 1000 kOhm over 150 kOhm with 1 uF (144 ms at its slowest), the
        average 0.1304 of the rail times (1 - the dominant share); the transceiver is silenced when its share passes 4.7 to 12.3 % (the
        rail at +-1.5 %, the resistors at 0.1 %, the threshold and the input current printed); at the legitimate 2 % it stays enabled: yes;
        SHDN driven to at least 2.27 V (VIH 2 V) by LIMO's 10 kOhm through a 1N4148W (0.715 V PRINTED at 1 mA, taken as the bound) into 100 kOhm,
        and held at 0.40 V (VIL 0.8 V) by that 100 kOhm against the pin's own 4 uA when nothing drives it; the controller's own SHDN
        request reaches the pin through the other diode. A held-dominant TXD is silenced within 16.0 ms (the driver's own time-out, 1.2 to
        3.8 ms PRINTED, frees the bus first); a babbler through its FDCAN, whose frames carry at least 15 % dominant bits (ASSUMED,
        FRAME_D_MIN: an all-recessive 8-byte frame carries about 24 dominant bits in 130), within 227 ms; the silence lasts while its
        TXD keeps the share over the limit and ends by itself when the share falls. A latent stuck comparator (OUTB held low) leaves that
        transceiver's share unbounded with nothing to find it in service: it weakens the service's containment (PROVISIONAL)
     2. THE RAIL TRIP, one per controller: 0.3 ohm from +5V_IOC to its LDO, the INA169 into 5.76 kOhm, a 1.17 s average (5.76 + 100 kOhm
        in the charging path, 10 uF,
        at its slowest), a TPS3701 holding the LDO's EN low while the average is over the threshold: 0.2183 to 0.2452 A at the tolerances;
        tripped, the controller is unpowered; the average then falls, the LDO restarts, and a controller still over the threshold is
        unpowered again: its supply's AVERAGE is held at the threshold (DERIVED); its peak is not (e). A latent rail trip (its monitor
        dead, its OUTB released) removes even that average bound with nothing to find it in service (PROVISIONAL)
        V-B23's response, as round 6 drafted it (EN low within 0.2 s of a 0.30 A load), is WITHDRAWN (cx46 6): from the bounded state the
        drafted network reaches the trip's maximum after 0.98 s (MODEL, the comparator's delay not counted); a corrected response mechanism
        and the complete network calculation are REMAINING ENGINEERING, protection not relaxed to obtain a pass
   (c) THE QUORUM AND RECOVERY, FAULT BY FAULT (quorum: two of three controllers serving; IOHA rows 3, 7 and 8), PROVISIONAL (cx46 5):
     a babbler through its FDCAN (FW-B21 broken), one or both fabrics its limiter silences its transceiver within 227 ms; the bus free; the other two                                        automatic: the limiter releases when its share falls
     a held-dominant TXD                                            the time-out frees the bus within 3.8 ms, the limiter silences it within 16.0 ms                                       automatic
     a clock or load outside FW-B20 (any firmware)                  the rail trip unpowers it, its average held at 0.2452 A or less; the other two                                         automatic: it restarts while its average is under the trip
     a fabric shorted, the firmware's response absent               its transceivers' share bounded by the limiter, the rail under the trip; the other fabric                              the fabric's repair
     a limiter's comparator dead, or its OUTB released              that transceiver silent: the controller on its other fabric; the quorum holds                                          found at once (its frames absent)
     a limiter's OUTB stuck low                                     that transceiver's share no longer bounded: LATENT, a second fault (a babbler) needed                                  bench V-B22; handed over (below)
     the rail trip's OUTB stuck low, or its monitor's output high   the controller unpowered: the other two                                                                                found at once
     the rail trip's monitor dead or its OUTB released              no current bound for that controller: LATENT, a second fault needed                                                    bench V-B23; handed over (below)
     one firmware fault in all three (a systematic fault)           each rail and each transceiver bounded on its own; the service may stop: the voters hold the home assignment (row 8)   the firmware's V-B20 to V-B22
     a CONTROLLER-DRIVEN babbler denies the bus at most for its detection time, 227 ms, the voters holding their assignment meanwhile
     (row 8), because its frames' dominant bits keep its share over the limit;
     WHAT IS NOT CLOSED (handed over as remaining engineering, no exception presumed): a TX pin repurposed as a GPIO and toggled under
     the limiter's least 4.7 % share disrupts the bus without tripping it; attributing it needs each controller's TXD read by the other
     two and a 2-of-2 vote of the other two on its SHDN or its LDO's EN (twelve observation inputs and six vote outputs, a pin plan for
     the three H743s): NOT DRAFTED here. And a latent stuck comparator in either bound, found only on the bench (V-B22, V-B23), with
     no service interval bounding that: the double faults. Outputs OPEN or PROVISIONAL on them: CON-004's quorum verdict (OPEN), FW-B22
     (PROVISIONAL), L9T5-F21 (OPEN) and this section's quorum rows. REMAINING ENGINEERING: an independent peer-silence or diagnostic
     circuit and the recovery proof. VOS0 under the trip takes the controller past its own 105 C VOS0 limit from 0.1936 A (MODEL), under
     the trip's band: it weakens the controller's survival and so FW-B20's and FW-B22's service (PROVISIONAL)
   (d) THE OTHER CONTROLLERS' HEADROOM DURING A RESPONSE: one controller at the worst current any firmware draws until its trip, 0.6776 A
